  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115894",
      "title": "Working with Inputs in Custom Directives",
      "lectureOrder": 157,
      "videoOrder": 149,
      "sourceHash": "88133610975328fd91cd8e4b51d880aa8312674bf658aa182b0ee7fc8518b2f1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 2.79,
          "en": "So we now saw how to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.79,
          "end": 6.18,
          "en": "and use a custom attribute directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.18,
          "end": 8.1,
          "en": "but I'm not done with that yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.1,
          "end": 12.6,
          "en": "because you can add more features to your own directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.6,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "because just like Components, they for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 20.39,
          "en": "also allow you to accept input values or emit outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 24.15,
          "en": "And I wanna accept an input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.15,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "because I actually wanna tweak the behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 31.473,
          "en": "of this directive a little bit, or change what it does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.43,
          "end": 37.43,
          "en": "To be precise when the user chooses to leave the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 44.3,
          "en": "I want to be able to add some analytics query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "to the address the user is about to navigate to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 52.8,
          "en": "So if a user, for example, clicks this first link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 52.8,
          "end": 55.2,
          "en": "and confirms that they want to go there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 60.2,
          "en": "I want to add a query parameter like from my app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 63.48,
          "en": "so that theoretically on that external page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.48,
          "end": 67.143,
          "en": "they could track this query parameter if they wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 68.07,
          "end": 71.61,
          "en": "Now, I don't wanna hardcode this here into this link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 71.61,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "which I could do, but I don't wanna do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "to keep these links here short and concise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 80.25,
          "en": "But I want to add that query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 80.25,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "when that directive here is active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 85.863,
          "en": "and the user confirmed that they wanna leave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "Now, how could we achieve this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.4,
          "end": 94.4,
          "en": "Well, by going back here to the SafeLink directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 97.17,
          "en": "And then as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.17,
          "end": 100.97999999999999,
          "en": "we need to get the address the user is about to navigate to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 100.97999999999999,
          "end": 102.273,
          "en": "if they wanna leave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 106.02000000000001,
          "en": "So we can get that address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "by accessing that event object, which we get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "And then there the target element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 115.5,
          "en": "which will be the anchor element which was clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.5,
          "end": 119.34,
          "en": "And therefore, there should be a href property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.34,
          "end": 121.14,
          "en": "on that target element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.14,
          "end": 124.26,
          "en": "which will hold that value that was set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 126.783,
          "en": "for this href attribute here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 130.56,
          "en": "Now TypeScript is not convinced here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.56,
          "end": 133.26,
          "en": "because it's not convinced that the event target",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 135.9,
          "en": "is necessarily an anchor element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.9,
          "end": 137.73,
          "en": "but we know that it should be,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.73,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "and we can therefore use a special TypeScript syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "which you haven't seen before to convince TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "We can use a feature called type costing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "where we add the ask keyword here after a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "for which we wanna change the TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 157.47,
          "en": "thinks this value is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.47,
          "end": 160.53,
          "en": "and tell TypeScript with which kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.53,
          "end": 161.673,
          "en": "we're dealing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 166.023,
          "en": "And here this is an HTML anchor element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 171.57,
          "en": "So by using this syntax, we convince TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.57,
          "end": 176.34,
          "en": "that event target will be of type HTML anchor element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.34,
          "end": 180.57,
          "en": "and then we can safely access the href property on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 182.973,
          "en": "to get the address we wanna navigate to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.83,
          "end": 189.83,
          "en": "Well, and with that done, we can change that address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "to be address plus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 196.59,
          "en": "and then we add the from query parameter like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.59,
          "end": 198.39,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.39,
          "end": 201.93,
          "en": "With that, that query parameter should be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.93,
          "end": 205.44,
          "en": "to the outgoing address when the user confirms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 206.643,
          "en": "that they wanna leave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.89,
          "end": 213.45,
          "en": "So with that, if we reload, if we click that first link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.45,
          "end": 214.77,
          "en": "and confirm this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.77,
          "end": 219.153,
          "en": "you see this query parameter was added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.02,
          "end": 222.06,
          "en": "so that's one way of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.06,
          "end": 223.38,
          "en": "But now, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.38,
          "end": 226.74,
          "en": "we wanna make that query parameter here configurable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.74,
          "end": 230.823,
          "en": "It shouldn't necessarily be my app all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.99,
          "end": 235.11,
          "en": "Instead, in the place where I'm using the directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.11,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "I'd like to set this dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 241.92,
          "en": "or at least I'd like to have the option of setting this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 244.11,
          "en": "So we could set this to my app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 244.11,
          "end": 249.11,
          "en": "but also to my app dash docs link, anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.68,
          "end": 255.68,
          "en": "And then here, maybe it's my app courses link, whatever.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 258.63,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "So I'd like to be able to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 264.93,
          "en": "different query parameter values here for that directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 264.93,
          "end": 269.67,
          "en": "or for that input that we're about to add to that directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 269.67,
          "end": 272.013,
          "en": "to make this directive configurable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 273.39,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "Well, as I mentioned, that's no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "because you can accept inputs in your Directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 281.223,
          "en": "just as you can do it on Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 284.86,
          "en": "You can do this with the add input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 286.05,
          "end": 288.33,
          "en": "or with the input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 288.33,
          "end": 291.06,
          "en": "Again, just as with Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 293.04,
          "en": "And here, I'll go for the input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 293.04,
          "end": 294.843,
          "en": "and not use the decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 295.77,
          "end": 298.44,
          "en": "Now, I'll add a new bindable input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 298.44,
          "end": 302.26,
          "en": "that could be named query param",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 305.67,
          "en": "and I turn it into an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 308.193,
          "en": "by using the input function here as mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 309.24,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "And I expect to get a string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 314.07,
          "en": "which should have a default value of my app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 314.07,
          "end": 317.52,
          "en": "So in case this input is not set, I want to use my app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 317.52,
          "end": 320.673,
          "en": "as a fallback here as a default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 323.31,
          "end": 327.24,
          "en": "And then down here where I assign that query parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 327.24,
          "end": 329.61,
          "en": "I will set the from query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 329.61,
          "end": 333.45,
          "en": "to the value this query param.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 333.45,
          "end": 336.27,
          "en": "And we need parentheses here, since this is a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 336.27,
          "end": 338.163,
          "en": "since I'm using the input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 340.62,
          "end": 342.87,
          "en": "With that, this would be configurable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.87,
          "end": 347.213,
          "en": "but it's configurable on an input called query param.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 348.65999999999997,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "So in the learning resources template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 355.89,
          "en": "we can't set it like this, but instead we add this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 355.89,
          "end": 360.89,
          "en": "and then we add this separate query param input like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 363.75,
          "end": 367.33,
          "en": "And I don't use square brackets around this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 368.46,
          "end": 370.11,
          "en": "input property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 370.11,
          "end": 372.99,
          "en": "because I'm not binding it to the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 372.99,
          "end": 375.78,
          "en": "of some dynamic TypeScript expression,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 375.78,
          "end": 377.7,
          "en": "but instead to a string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 377.7,
          "end": 380.1,
          "en": "And as you learned earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 380.1,
          "end": 383.37,
          "en": "if you're setting some hardcoded string value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 383.37,
          "end": 385.8,
          "en": "as a value for an input property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 385.8,
          "end": 388.5,
          "en": "you don't need that property binding syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 388.5,
          "end": 392.4,
          "en": "with square brackets because that would just turn this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 392.4,
          "end": 395.73,
          "en": "between the quotes here into some TypeScript expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 395.73,
          "end": 397.11,
          "en": "instead of a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 397.11,
          "end": 398.76,
          "en": "and I don't want that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 398.76,
          "end": 401.31,
          "en": "I want a hardcoded string value instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 401.31,
          "end": 402.14300000000003,
          "en": "So therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 402.14300000000003,
          "end": 404.553,
          "en": "I'm setting this input property like this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 406.77,
          "end": 409.65,
          "en": "But with that, if you save all that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 409.65,
          "end": 413.01,
          "en": "if you go back and you click that first link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 413.01,
          "end": 417.51,
          "en": "and you confirm this, you see my app docs link was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 417.51,
          "end": 419.163,
          "en": "as a query parameter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 420.36,
          "end": 423.873,
          "en": "If you click that second link and confirm this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 424.77,
          "end": 429.543,
          "en": "you see my app courses link was added as a query parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 431.76,
          "end": 433.29,
          "en": "So that works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 433.29,
          "end": 438.24,
          "en": "and it proves that you can add inputs to your Directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 438.24,
          "end": 442.56,
          "en": "However, it is quite common that you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 442.56,
          "end": 447.06,
          "en": "to simplify the usage of attribute Directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 447.06,
          "end": 450.63,
          "en": "and you therefore might want to allow yourself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 450.63,
          "end": 454.29,
          "en": "to set that query parameter value like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 454.29,
          "end": 458.4,
          "en": "as a value for an input that has the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 458.4,
          "end": 461.073,
          "en": "as your directive selector here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 462.84000000000003,
          "end": 464.4,
          "en": "And currently, this wouldn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 464.4,
          "end": 468.3,
          "en": "because we have no input called app SafeLink.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 468.3,
          "end": 471.54,
          "en": "But of course we could change this name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 471.54,
          "end": 474.09000000000003,
          "en": "or if you want to keep query param",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 474.09000000000003,
          "end": 479.09000000000003,
          "en": "as a name here in this class, we could assign an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 479.43,
          "end": 482.76,
          "en": "by passing this configuration object to the input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 482.76,
          "end": 486.22,
          "en": "and setting an alias of app SafeLink",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 488.55,
          "end": 492.87,
          "en": "so that this input internally has the name query param",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 492.87,
          "end": 497.13,
          "en": "but externally in the place where the directive is applied,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 497.13,
          "end": 498.603,
          "en": "it has this name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 500.1,
          "end": 503.25,
          "en": "And that would now allow us to set the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 503.25,
          "end": 505.71,
          "en": "for this query parameter as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 505.71,
          "end": 508.47,
          "en": "for an input called app SafeLink",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 508.47,
          "end": 512.103,
          "en": "in the place where we're applying this directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 514.17,
          "end": 517.41,
          "en": "So with that, if you save this, if you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 517.41,
          "end": 521.913,
          "en": "you'll see that still, this value is being used.",
